lesson: 249
title: Weight and volume in the kitchen
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A litre is 1000 millilitres, and a kilogram is 1000 grams.
explain: To find what is left in a carton, turn the litres into millilitres, add up everything poured out, and take it away.
explain: A 2 litre carton is 2000 ml. After 4 glasses of 200 ml and a 150 ml cup, 2000 - 800 - 150 = 1050 ml are left.
vars: a=name b=name l=2..3 g=2..6 c=3..6 w=50..250 z=2..9
let: v = c * 50
need: w % 10 == 0
need: g * v + w < l * 1000
answer: l * 1000 - g * v - w
exercise: A carton holds {l} litres of milk. {a} pours {g} glasses of {v} ml each and then {w} ml into a cake mix. How many millilitres of milk are left?
exercise: {a} has a {l} litre bottle of juice. {a.He} fills {g} cups of {v} ml each and pours {w} ml for the baby. How many millilitres remain in the bottle?
exercise: A jug holds {l} litres of water. Mum fills {g} glasses of {v} ml and waters a plant with {w} ml. How much water, in millilitres, is still in the jug?
exercise: {a} makes pancakes from a {l} kg bag of flour. {a.He} uses {g} scoops of {v} g each and then {w} g more for dusting. How many grams of flour are left in the bag?
exercise: There are {l} kg of rice in a bag. Dad cooks {g} portions of {v} g each and gives {w} g to a neighbour. How many grams of rice are left?
exercise: {l} litre milk, {a} poured {g} glasses {v} ml each plus {w} ml in the porridge. how many ml left
exercise: we had {l} kg of sugar, used {g} lots of {v} grams for jam, oh and {w+10} — no {w} g in tea. grams left?
exercise: {a} drank {g} glasses of {v} ml from the {l} litre carton, then spilt like {w} ml lol. how much left in ml
exercise: {b} says a {l} litre bottle minus {g} cups of {v} ml and {w} ml leaves {l*100-g*v/10-w/10} ml. that's wrong innit? how many ml really
exercise: {l} kg flour bag, {g} batches of cookies at {v} g each and {w} g for the gravy. how many g left
exercise: mum's {l} L of orange juice, {g} glasses {v} ml each, {w} ml for the dog's... no, for the punch. how much left ml
test: How many millilitres remain in a {l} litre carton once {g} glasses holding {v} ml each and a further {w} ml have been poured from it?
test: {a} bakes {g} loaves, each needing {v} g of flour, and thickens a sauce with {w} g. The flour came from a {l} kg bag. What mass of flour, in grams, is left?
test: From a {l} litre bottle of lemonade, {a} serves {g} friends {v} ml each and keeps {w} ml for {b}. A straw costs {z} cents. How many millilitres are left in the bottle?
test: {w} ml went into the soup and {g} mugs of {v} ml were filled, all from a {l} litre carton of stock. How much stock is left, in ml?
test: {l} kg potatoes, cooked {g} lots of {v} g n another {w} g for chips. g left?
test: {l} litre of milk, {g} bowls of cereal at {v} ml each and {w} ml for the cat. ml left pls
exam: Determine the volume, in millilitres, remaining in a vessel of {l.words} litres capacity following the withdrawal of {g.words} measures of {v} ml each and a further {w} ml.
exam: It is given that a bag containing {l} kilograms of flour is subjected to the removal of {g} portions of {v} grams and a subsequent quantity of {w} grams. Ascertain the mass of flour remaining, expressed in grams.
exam: A carton of {l} litres having been diminished by {g} servings of {v} ml apiece and by {w} ml in addition, state the residual volume in millilitres.
exam: Whereas {a} dispenses {g} glasses of {v} ml and subsequently {w} ml from a container holding {l} litres, compute the quantity of liquid, in millilitres, remaining therein.
exercise: Grandma is not as young as she was, so {a} helps her: from a {l} litre bottle of milk {a.he} fills {g} mugs of {v} ml each and then pours {w} ml into the custard. How many millilitres are left?
exercise: {a} poured {g} glasses of {v} ml from the {l} litre carton, then {b} helped {b.him}self, nicked {w} ml of the bloody juice straight from it. how many ml left, then?
test: Dad, who was let go at the factory last month, now cooks at home. From {l} litres of stock he ladles {g} bowls of {v} ml and stirs {w} ml into the rice. What volume remains, in millilitres?
